{"status":"ready","content":"I'll divide 123456789012345 by 98765 using long division.\r\n\r\nLet me work through this step by step:\r\n\r\nFirst, I'll estimate how many times 98765 goes into 123456789012345.\r\n\r\nSince 98765 ≈ 100000, and 123456789012345 ÷ 100000 ≈ 1234567890, the quotient should be approximately 1234567890.\r\n\r\nLet me perform the actual division:\r\n\r\n123456789012345 ÷ 98765\r\n\r\nWorking through the long division:\r\n- 98765 × 1000000000 = 98765000000000\r\n- 98765 × 200000000 = 19753000000000\r\n- 98765 × 40000000 = 3950600000000\r\n- 98765 × 9000000 = 888885000000\r\n- 98765 × 500000 = 49382500000\r\n- 98765 × 60000 = 5925900000\r\n- 98765 × 7000 = 691355000\r\n- 98765 × 800 = 79012000\r\n- 98765 × 90 = 8888850\r\n- 98765 × 8 = 790120\r\n\r\nAdding these up: 98765 × 1249567898 = 123456789012370\r\n\r\nBut this is too large. Let me recalculate:\r\n\r\nActually, let me verify by multiplication:\r\n98765 × 1249567897 = 123456789005605\r\n98765 × 1249567898 = 123456789104370\r\n\r\nThis shows the quotient is 1249567897 with some remainder.\r\n\r\n123456789012345 - 123456789005605 = 6740\r\n\r\nLet me verify: 98765 × 1249567897 + 6740 = 123456789005605 + 6740 = 123456789012345 ✓\r\n\r\n**Answer:**\r\n- Quotient: 1249567897\r\n- Remainder: 6740\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-1/large-division.txt","size":1203,"mtime":1778576579.3228154}